  "notes": [
    "Broad topic and programming-language search seeds improve coverage but cannot enumerate every repository on GitHub.",
    "GitHub Search API caps results per query and applies separate rate limits; each query is paginated only to the configured page cap.",
    "Forks are not excluded by default because useful independent work can exist in forks; duplicates are handled as review hints.",
    "Archived repositories remain discoverable and must be labelled accurately during review.",
    "Only public repository metadata is collected. Private repositories and private user data are out of scope.",
    "Candidates are never added to the public catalogue automatically.",
    "Additional Forgejo/Gitea instances are opt-in. Add only reviewed public hosts with HTTPS origin URLs and public unauthenticated API access. Empty by default.",
    "npm and crates.io are searched through their official public registry APIs. Only records with an approved public source-repository URL are converted into repository candidates; registry-only packages without a source link are not added to this queue.",
    "RubyGems discovery uses the public search API and only queues explicit metadata.source_code_uri values on approved repository hosts. NuGet and Maven Central remain planned until a reliable source-repository enrichment step is designed."
